My second ascension! I went with a Neutral Human Barbarian this time
(my 1st was a Valkyrie). This game actually started out rather poorly,
as I couldn't find a bag or a light source for *ages*. I actually never
did complete the Gnomish mines, as I got tired of wandering around in
the dark. I had to really concentrate on keeping a portable base (a
large chest named Treasure Chest) since my carrying capacity was so
terrible. Good thing I was playing a class with good strength!

I found some Gauntlets of Dexterity fairly early on, and a +5 Dwarven
Helm in the Gnome Mines (which I wore till the end). There was a Magic
Marker in the first few levels, which was very helpful for identifying
and enchanting my armor/weapon. I did some sacrificing and was declared
the Envoy of Balance when I was level 14, and got a Vorpal Blade to go
with the Shield of Reflection I had found (previously I was using a +4
battleaxe).

I did some alchemy before I entered Gehennom, and came out with 12
blessed Full Healing potions, bringing my HP up to the upper 200s, and
left 3 for the endgame.

I finally found a plain sack off of Perseus' statue (yeah, THAT long
before I found a bag) so I could at least carry a decent number of
items, and a lamp around Gehennom level 5. I penned a stack of Magic
Mapping scrolls and sped through Gehennom as fast as I could, which
hurt my score by about 2 million at the end :(. Oh well, an ascension
is an ascension!

The mysterious force was initially pretty merciful, but at level 36 got
really brutal. I finally got back to my base on Medusa's Isle and
swapped out everything I'd need for the endgame, and got to going
upstairs. The planes were really easy since I had potions of confusion
and scrolls of gold detection, but I had to quaff 2 full healing
potions on Air as I kept getting enveloped.

Onto the Astral plane, I was wearing Conflict (which I hadn't tried
before), wow does that make a difference! I went right, opened the
door, and Death was staring at me -- So, I turned around and went
middle. Just after I walked through the middle door, I got Aggrivated
at the Priest of Crom (my guy!), in the middle temple. What fortune!
Truly the gods did smile upon me in that moment. Zapped a teleport wand
straight ahead to cut a way through the foes, opened the door, and
#offered.

Invisible choir :). WOOT!

